{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.5,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "wrong_value",
      "components": ["R3", "R4"],
      "pins": ["J11.3", "J5.3", "U2.6", "U2.7"],
      "nets": ["NET0038", "NET0028", "/PWM1", "/PWM2"],
      "observed": "There is no 1 kΩ resistor anywhere on the sheet. The series path from the selected PWM bus net (NET0038 / NET0028) to the servo signal pin (J11 pin 3 / J5 pin 3) is a 0 Ω jumper, and the same 0 Ω node is also tied straight to the MAX3485 A/B lines, so the PWM signal pin is hard-wired to the transceiver bias network with no series resistance.",
      "expected": "The specification requires 1 kΩ series resistors (R3, R4) between the PWM1/PWM2 GPIO nets and the servo signal pins: 'R3, R4 | 1k each | Series resistors from the PWM1/PWM2 GPIO nets to J3 pin 3 / J8 pin 3 respectively', and §3 states PWM mode gives 'its own independent 1 kΩ-buffered GPIO line'.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "R3, R4 | 1k each | Series resistors from the PWM1/PWM2 GPIO nets to J3 pin 3 / J8 pin 3 respectively."},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "each servo header's signal pin gets its own independent 1 kΩ-buffered GPIO line (/PWM1 → J3 pin3, /PWM2 → J8 pin3)"},
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "Right cluster: NET0038 —[0 Ω]— J11.3 and NET0028 —[0 Ω]— J5.3; no 1 kΩ value present on the sheet (only 0, 2k, 2.2k, 5.1k, 10k, 20k, 47k)."}
      ],
      "impact": "In PWM mode the servo signal lines lose their intended series buffering/current-limiting and are loaded by the MAX3485 A/B bias network (2.2 kΩ pull-ups), altering the drive characteristics of the PWM channels relative to the intended independent 1 kΩ-buffered lines.",
      "confidence": 0.5
    },
    {
      "category": "wrong_component_type",
      "components": ["C5", "C2"],
      "pins": ["U2.8", "U2.6", "U2.7"],
      "nets": ["+3V3", "NET0038", "NET0018"],
      "observed": "The only 0.1 µF capacitor (C2) is connected between the MAX3485 differential pins (U2 pin 6 A and U2 pin 7 B); there is no 0.1 µF decoupling capacitor from U2 VCC (pin 8) to GND.",
      "expected": "The specification lists C5 as a 0.1 µF decoupling capacitor on the +3V3 supply of the MAX3485: 'C5 | 0.1 µF | Decoupling cap on +3V3 (MAX3485 supply).'",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "C5 | 0.1 µF | Decoupling cap on +3V3 (MAX3485 supply)."},
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "C2 0.1u drawn vertically between the A and B line nodes of U2; U2 pin 8 (VCC) connects only to the +3V3 arrow with no local 0.1 µF cap."}
      ],
      "impact": "The MAX3485 supply is left undecoupled (risk of supply noise / brownout during TX), and a 0.1 µF across the differential pair heavily loads the serial bus capacitively, degrading the half-duplex serial servo signal in Serial mode.",
      "confidence": 0.35
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The build deviates from the specification in the servo signal path: the intended 1 kΩ PWM series resistors (R3/R4) are absent (the signal pins are tied to the PWM/RS-485 nets through 0 Ω jumpers), and the 0.1 µF MAX3485 supply decoupling cap is not on +3V3 but instead appears across the A/B lines, both of which change the board's PWM/serial behaviour from what was intended."
}

